the $△\\,NPQ$, if $N(1,0,1)$, $P(2,2,3)$, $Q(2,1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{NP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{NQ}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{NP} & =p-n \\\\  & =(2i+2j+3k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{NQ} & =q-n \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{NP}\\times \\overset{\\to }{NQ} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)i-(1\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{NP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{NQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{NP}\\times \\overset{\\to }{NQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,NPQ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5c5db25945cf065904539ec2f51ea16f35ef136d3df2b95fcc938e9fc1fca9f"} {"question" "q-71107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $ZH$ of the $△\\,WYZ$, if $W(2,3,2)$, $Y(1,2,1)$, $Z(1,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $ZH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,WYZ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY\n$$\n\nSo, to find $ZH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WZ}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-(2i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WZ} & =z-w \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(2i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-4j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WY}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WZ} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))j+((-1)\\cdot (-4)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WZ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WY}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WZ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WYZ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $WY$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}WY & =|\\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =ZH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ ZH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ZH & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5c5db25945cf065904539ec2f51ea16f35ef136d3df2b95fcc938e9fc1fca9f"} {"question" "q-71116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-71116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY,$ if $W(3,9,4),$ $X(1,7,3),$ $Y(6,12,8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(i+7j+3k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(6i+12j+8k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))i-((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))j+((-2)\\cdot 3-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-5i+5j \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5c5db25945cf065904539ec2f51ea16f35ef136d3df2b95fcc938e9fc1fca9f"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-128008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $RH$ of the $△\\,PRQ,$ if $P(3,0,4),$ $Q(2,3,1),$ $R(0,3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-128008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $RH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,PQR$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $RH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3j-3j \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-3)\\cdot (-3))j+((-1)\\cdot 3-(-3)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $PQ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 6\\sqrt{2} & =RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-128008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5c5db25945cf065904539ec2f51ea16f35ef136d3df2b95fcc938e9fc1fca9f"} {"question" "q-128008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065453/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4a975719eb4442217acafcdb9e97baebacf667b0c631b5184425470c4b4524a"} {"question" "q-128008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\